cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LISPMIND: An Autonomous, Self-Healing Multi-Agent Platform for Distributed System Resilience"
abstract: >
  LISPMIND is a research platform for autonomous, self-healing multi-agent
  systems implemented in Common Lisp. It demonstrates novel techniques in
  runtime strategy evolution, multi-tier fault tolerance, hardware-bound
  credential management, and low-bandwidth distributed coordination within
  a single, long-running Lisp image. The system combines genetic programming,
  CLOS metaobject protocol hooks, kernel-level system monitoring, and
  encrypted resource vaults to create an autonomous computing organism.
authors:
  - family-names: "LISPMIND Research Collective"
    affiliation: "Independent Security Research"
